   "tutor": "Rule: put the doer first, then the action, then the thing; put place or time at the end.\nRight: \"The farmer feeds the cows.\" Wrong: \"Feeds the farmer the cows.\" The wrong one puts the action before the doer.\nWorked example: words \"eats / a banana / the monkey\". Step 1: who does it? The monkey. Step 2: the action: eats. Step 3: the thing: a banana. Result: \"The monkey eats a banana.\"\nNow you. Put in order: \"plays / Sam / chess / on Mondays\"",
